# Core Mathematical Reformulation

Use the ball-covering interpretation of burning.

A burning sequence of length q corresponds to covering V(T) by balls with radii

$$
q-1,q-2,\ldots,1,0.
$$

Thus

$$
b(T)\le q
$$

is equivalent to the existence of a covering

$$
V(T)\subseteq
B(v_1,q-1)\cup
B(v_2,q-2)\cup\cdots\cup
B(v_q,0).
$$

The desired contrapositive says:

> If no such q-ball covering exists, then T must contain at least 2q-1 degree-2 vertices.

Find a way to make this implication structural.

