# Suggested Structural Decomposition

Suppress all degree-2 vertices of T.

Let H be the resulting topological core.

Each edge e of H corresponds to a path in T containing some number

$$
s_e\ge0
$$

of degree-2 vertices.

Therefore

$$
n_2(T)=\sum_{e\in E(H)}s_e.
$$

Study T as:

$$
T=(H;\{s_e\}_{e\in E(H)}).
$$

Ask whether a q-round burning obstruction imposes constraints on the subdivision lengths \(s_e\).

